  "nl_text": "The database schema for the database named 'rschema_0255' consists of 11 tables. The database is used for managing various aspects of a manufacturing process, from equipment inspections and failures to quality reports and user management.\nThe 'production_report' table represents the production reports generated by the production team. It contains columns for the report type, date, production data, production indicators, completion status, metal recovery rate, and grade. The report_id is the primary key.\nThe 'equipment' table holds information about the various types of equipment used in the manufacturing process. It includes columns for equipment name, model, main category, subcategory, location, and operation status. The equipment_id is the primary key.\nThe 'equipment_inspection' table records the details of equipment inspections. It includes columns for equipment_id, inspector_id, inspection plan, and execution progress. The combination of inspector_id and equipment_id forms the primary key. The foreign keys are linked to the 'user' and 'equipment' tables respectively.\nThe 'equipment_failure_reporting' table records the details of equipment failures. It includes columns for equipment_id, failure_reporter_id, failure type, failure time, and processing status. The combination of failure_reporter_id and equipment_id forms the primary key. The foreign keys are linked to the 'user' and 'equipment' tables respectively.\nThe 'equipment_repair' table records the details of equipment repairs. It includes columns for equipment_id, repair_person_id, repair progress, and repair time. The primary key is repair_id. The foreign keys are linked to the 'user' and 'equipment' tables respectively.\nThe 'quality_report' table holds the quality reports generated by the quality team. It includes columns for metal recovery rate, warehouse sample, metal grade, recovery rate daily report, and grade daily report. The report_id is the primary key.\nThe 'equipment_monitoring' table records the details of equipment monitoring. It includes columns for equipment_id, equipment type, collected data, status, monitoring data, fault alarm, data visualization, and administrator_id. The combination of equipment_id and administrator_id forms the primary key. The foreign keys are linked to the 'user' and 'equipment' tables respectively.\nThe 'user' table holds information about the users of the system. It includes columns for user_id, username, role, permissions, status, and operation history. The user_id is the primary key.\nThe 'announcement' table holds information about announcements made by users. It includes columns for announcement_id, announcement content, release time, publisher_id, and announcement status. The announcement_id is the primary key. The foreign key is linked to the 'user' table.\nThe 'job_position' table holds information about job positions available. It includes columns for job_id, job name, job description, job responsibilities, and job requirements. The job_id is the primary key.\nThe 'user_job_application' table holds information about user job applications. It includes columns for user_id, job_id, and job match rate. The combination of user_id and job_id forms the primary key. The foreign keys are linked to the 'user' and 'job_position' tables respectively.\nAll tables allow null values except for the NOT NULL constraints. Default values are not specified. Primary keys are unique and not null, and foreign keys are used to link tables together. The ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE options are used to handle deletions and updates in the linked tables.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description :\n1.Production Statistics:\nProduction reports, displaying production data for each process. Information to be recorded includes the report type, date, production data, production indicators, completion status, metal recovery rate, and grade.\n2.Equipment Management:\nEquipment record management, including basic information (name, model, main category, subcategory, location, etc.). Equipment operation status, with real-time monitoring and alarm notifications in case of anomalies.\nEquipment inspection management, recording inspection plans and progress, performed by the inspector.\nEquipment failure reporting, recording information about the failure, including the reporter’s ID, failure type, failure time, and processing status.\nEquipment repair management, handled by repair personnel, recording repair details and progress, and managing repair work orders. Information such as repair progress and repair time should be recorded.\n3.Quality Management:\nQuality report module, displaying the recovery rate and grade for each metal. Records to include metal recovery rate, incoming warehouse sample, metal grade, recovery rate daily report, and grade daily report.\n4.User Management:\nFor each user in the system, the following details should be recorded: user ID, username, role, permissions, status, and operation history.\n5.Announcements:\nAnnouncers can create, publish, delete, and retrieve announcements. Information to record includes announcement content, release time, and announcement status.\n6.Job Positions:\nThe system should register currently available job positions, including position ID, position name, position description, position responsibilities, and job requirements. Users can apply for positions, and the system will record the position match rate.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0255.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0255\nCREATE TABLE `production_report` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `report_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `report_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `production_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `production_indicators` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `completion_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `metal_recovery_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `main_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `subcategory` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_inspection` (\n  `inspector_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_plan` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `execution_progress` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inspector_id`, `equipment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_inspection_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`inspector_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_inspection_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_failure_reporting` (\n  `failure_reporter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `failure_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processing_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`failure_reporter_id`, `equipment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_failure_reporting_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`failure_reporter_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_failure_reporting_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_repair` (\n  `repair_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `repair_person_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `repair_progress` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `repair_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`repair_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_repair_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`repair_person_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_repair_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `quality_report` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `metal_recovery_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `warehouse_sample` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `metal_grade` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recovery_rate_daily_report` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade_daily_report` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_monitoring` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `collected_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `monitoring_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fault_alarm` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `data_visualization` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`, `administrator_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_monitoring_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_monitoring_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `permissions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_history` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `announcement_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `release_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `announcement_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `job_position` (\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_responsibilities` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_requirements` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_job_application` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_match_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `job_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_job_application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_job_application_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_id`) REFERENCES `job_position` (`job_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
